dialect protocol
protocol svg.diff
version 1
schema stdio.svg
start record

# P2-FG3: REAL binary diff frame, replacing F6's `print_diff().into_bytes()` text-as-binary
# shortcut (`../../🦀️.rs`'s old `DiffCodec::encode_diff` -- per the P2-W0 census, 100% of
# stdio's `DiffCodec` impls were still on this shortcut). `format u8` + `flags u8` (bit0 =
# `declaration` present, bit1 = `doctype` present, bit2 = `root` present, bit3 = `prolog`
# present) as two REAL fixed fields, individually protocol-walked.
#
# Past that header, `declaration`/`doctype`/`root` (whichever `flags` marks present, in that FIXED
# order) are bundled into ONE opaque trailing `bytes` chain rather than three separately-declared
# conditional fields: this dialect's `Cond` (`if flags eq N`) can only test a field's WHOLE value
# against a literal, not an individual BIT of it (no bitwise-AND primitive exists,
# `📖️grammar-recipe.md` §2.2's own `Cond` section), so a per-bit-guarded field list isn't
# expressible here even before `root`'s own recursion is considered. And `root`'s own payload
# (`SvgNodeDiff`, a genuinely recursive, data-carrying enum) hits the SAME `protocol-prim-ref-
# recursion` mechanism gap every other stdio artifact's diff/mutation payload hits (`Prim::Ref`
# unconditionally errors in `walk_protocol` -- confirmed unchanged through every pilot) -- so once
# ANY field of this frame is structurally unwalkable, bundling the two simpler, merely-optional
# fields (`declaration`/`doctype`) into the SAME opaque tail, instead of partially structuring only
# those two, is the honest, minimal-surface choice: the Rust `encode_diff`/`decode_diff` side stays
# genuinely, fully structured (bit-tested, individually typed) and round-trip tested independently.
framing record
header fixed 2
field format u8
field flags u8
chain payload bytes
